      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`TraceCustomIdGenerator` has two problems with the IDs it generates:\n\n- Trace IDs come from `getrandbits(64)`, so the upper half of the 128-bit W3C trace ID is always zero.\n- Each process seeds its own `random.Random` with `time.time()`. Processes started at the same clock reading, such as the TP scheduler processes of one server, draw identical ID sequences, so their trace and span IDs can collide. Avoiding collisions across scheduler processes is why this custom generator exists.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Draw IDs from `random.SystemRandom` (the OS entropy pool), so there is no seed to collide on.\n- Trace IDs are 128-bit. Span IDs stay 64-bit, as W3C trace context requires.\n- Skip the all-zero ID, which is invalid in W3C trace context.\n- Preset span IDs for async tracing (`preset_next_span_id`) are unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: tracing only, no change to model outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n`SystemRandom` adds about 1 µs per ID (`getrandbits(64)`: ~1.2 µs vs ~0.2 µs with `random.Random`). IDs are drawn only for traced requests: one trace ID per request and one span ID per span.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_trace.py::TestTraceCustomIdGenerator::test_trace_ids_use_all_128_bits`: trace IDs are non-zero and use the upper 64 bits.\n- `test_trace.py::TestTraceCustomIdGenerator::test_generators_created_at_the_same_instant_draw_different_ids`: with `time.time` frozen, two generators draw different IDs. The previous generator, re-seeded from the clock, draws identical ones.\n- End to end on 2× L4 (Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct, TP=2, spans exported to Jaeger): all 8 engine-started traces had non-zero upper 64 bits.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (Not needed: no user-facing change.)\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (Not applicable: no model-output change; overhead above.)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38970301374](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38970301374)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38970301339](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38970301339)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38970301448](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38970301448)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
